  "Source variant note (not a gap): Example 4.6.11 in the source uses Z_n in {0,n} with P(Z_n=n)=1/n; the handbook writes X_n=nB_nC_n with Bernoulli C_n, an equivalent reparametrisation, and computes the tail mean 1/n instead of the source's E(X_n;|X_n|>=1)=n/n^2.",
  "Exercise 4.6.4 hypothesis: source quantifies over every real x with delta(x); body line 276-281 quantifies over positive integers K. This is equivalent because {X_n<=x} is contained in {X_n<=ceil(x)}; noted only for fidelity reviewers.",
  "thm:p15-extinction-or-escape (body 273) requires finite nonnegative X_n, while the branching application (annex 496) establishes finiteness only almost surely; a modification on a null set is implicit. Correctness/precision remark only, not a coverage gap.",
